  },
  // Afternoon
  {
    time: "12:45 PM",
    title: "Cool Demo, Bro. Now Ship It: Why Most GenAI Apps Fall Apart",
    description: "Katie Novotny",
    abstract: "Everyone has a GenAI demo. Very few have a GenAI system. In this talk, we'll roast the most common GenAI anti-patterns - chatbots pretending to be apps, agents with no guardrails, and \"just add RAG\" architectures that collapse under real users. Then we'll rebuild them the right way. You'll learn how production GenAI actually works: tools over prompts, systems over models, and architectures that assume failure, hallucination, and chaos from day one. We'll cover when agents are useful (and when they're absolutely not), why observability matters more for AI than traditional services, and how to ship GenAI without lighting your cloud bill on fire. This is not a hype talk. This is a survival guide."
  },
  {
    time: "1:30 PM",
    title: "Break",
    description: "15 minutes"
  },
  {
    time: "1:45 PM",
    title: "Session TBA",
    description: "Ian Taylor"
  },
